course: dictionary
lesson: 6375
title: Muffle and the clues around it
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Context means the words around a word. Its clues can help you work out what an unknown word means. «Owl wing feathers have soft fringes and a velvety surface that muffle the sound of flying.» Soft fringes and velvet are soft things, so muffle must mean making a sound quieter.
explain: «Your dog gives tiny muffled woofs.» Tiny tells you the woofs are small and quiet, and muffled tells you they are also hard to hear clearly. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Muffle has a second meaning too. To muffle someone up is to wrap them in warm clothes or cloth, as in «muffled up against the cold». The clue is the cold: you wrap up warm when it is cold.
fact: To muffle a sound means to make it quieter and less clear.
fact: «Muffled voices» means voices that come through something, like a wall, and are hard to hear clearly.
fact: Soft materials such as foam, cloth and egg boxes muffle sound by absorbing its vibrations.
fact: To muffle someone up means to wrap them in warm clothes or cloth.
exercise: «The soft fringes on the owl's wings muffle the sound of flying.» What does muffle mean here? | Stop the owl from ever flying | Make the sound louder and sharper | *Make the sound quieter and less clear | Make the owl fly faster
exercise: Mum says, «Wrap up warm, we're going out in the snow, so let's muffle you up.» What does muffle you up mean? | Shout at you to hurry | Paint your face for a game | *Wrap you in warm clothes | Cover you with mud
exercise: In a science test, Priya covers a ringing bell with a thick cloth. What does the cloth do to the sound? | Changes the colour of the bell | Makes the sound higher | Makes the sound louder | *Makes the sound quieter and less clear
test: «The snow muffled our footsteps as we walked home.» What does muffled mean here? | *Quiet and hard to hear clearly | Very fast | Frozen solid | Loud and clear
test: In a science lesson, which material would best muffle sound? | Metal spoon | *Thick foam | Glass jar | Sharp pencil
exam: «Glue ear is sticky fluid behind the eardrum that muffles sound.» What does muffles mean in this sentence? | *Makes sound quieter and less clear | Makes sound louder and sharper | Makes the eardrum dry | Makes the sound stop completely
